    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nI am using the mini.files plugin and would like to restrict navigation such that when using the go_out() function, I want to prevent navigation outside the initial directory from which mini.files was opened. I have attempted to implement it myself, but it seems to not work as expected.\r\n\r\nIn other words I would like the plugin to restrict navigation so that when I try to go up from the initial directory, it prevents me from going outside this directory.",
