    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nI think the best approach here would be via custom mapping which would essentially:\r\n- Do nothing is currently focused path is the initial (anchor) directory.\r\n- Execute `go_out()` otherwise.\r\n\r\nThe main issue here is programmatically determining what is the the anchor directory for currently opened explorer. It *can* mostly be done inside 'MiniFilesExplorerOpen' event (via calling `get_fs_entry()` and computing its directory name), but it is a bit cumbersome and not 100% reliable. I'll think about making it more straightforward.",
