        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> vim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"h\", custom_go_out, { noremap = true, silent = true })\r\n\r\nMaking a global mapping like that is probably not a good idea. I'd recommend adapting [this example](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/a8185957febe7dae31556dbd7326cfa597b812f1/doc/mini-files.txt#L450-L457) and create a buffer-local mapping inside autocommand for `MiniFilesBufferCreate` event. This would mean moving all the helper logic inside `MiniFilesExplorerOpen` autocommand.\r\n\r\nI do plan to make this use case a bit more straightforward. Probably, by introducing `get_explorer_data()` function which can be used to get anchor path without the need of 'MiniFilesExplorerOpen' workaround.",
